      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:8:7",
      "text": [
        " صَلَّى فِي مَسْجِدِ الْخَيْفِ سَبْعُمِائَةِ نَبِيٍّ وَ إِنَّ مَا بَيْنَ الرُّكْنِ وَ الْمَقَامِ لَمَشْحُونٌ مِنْ قُبُورِ الْأَنْبِيَاءِ وَ إِنَّ آدَمَ لَفِي حَرَمِ اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ibn Abu Najran, from Al Mufazzal, from Jabir, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Seven hundred Prophets<sup>as</sup> have Prayed in Masjid Al-Khief, and that what is in between the corner (of the Kaaba) and the Standing Place (of Ibrahim<sup>as</sup>) is fraught with the graves of the Prophets<sup>as</sup>, and that Adam<sup>as</sup> is in the Sanctuary of Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "7. A number of our people have narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from ibn abu Najran from al-Mufaddal from Jabir who has said the following: “Abu Ja’far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Seven hundred prophets said salat (prayer) in the Masjid of al-Khif, in Mina. The area between the corner and al-Maqam (the station of Ibrahim) is full of the graves of prophets; and Adam is in the Sacred place of Allah, the Most Majestic, the Most Glorious.” "
        ]
      }
    },
